This repository includes material adapted from Anthropic's claude-plugins-official,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

  https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official
  plugins/code-simplifier/agents/code-simplifier.md

skills/code-simplifier/SKILL.md quotes and adapts that agent's guidance for OpenCode
and adds a parallel-review workflow. The files were modified for OpenCode: the agent
frontmatter, tool names, and the CLAUDE.md reference were changed.

The parallel three-subagent review pass is inspired by Claude Code's /simplify command.

This repository also includes material adapted from Anthropic's claude-code-security-review,
licensed under the MIT License:

  https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code-security-review
  claudecode/prompts.py

skills/code-security-review/code-security-review.md draws on that prompt's high-confidence
reporting rules — the minimize-false-positives bar, the confidence threshold, and the
excluded issue types — and rewrites the workflow for OpenCode. Its differential scope and
false-positive-verification approach are inspired by the Trail of Bits skills (CC-BY-SA-4.0).
